      "message": "[warning] Line 46: 🟡 Clearing `fixedTransform` now forces `currentTransform` to `.identity`. If `fixedTransform` is removed while the stream is paused/low-FPS, `syncGeometry()` immediately applies identity and PiP can show the video with the wrong orientation until a new frame arrives and recomputes transform in `render(_:)`. Keep the previous `currentTransform` when `newValue \u003d\u003d nil`, or recompute from `lastFrame` before calling `syncGeometry()` so orientation stays stable between frames.",
